  "title": "A record save that writes or removes the record's view SQL moves SRM by 1 as well as RDM",
  "statement": "When a record save creates, rewrites or removes the record's SQL definition (SQL View, Materialized View, Dynamic View text: PSSQLDEFN SQLTYPE 2), App Designer bumps PSVERSION and PSLOCK SRM by one besides RDM and SYS. A save that leaves the SQL rows alone does not (r62, Derived/Work to Dynamic View with no text, wrote none and moved no SRM). A removal writes PSSQLDEL at the new SRM (r58, r60).",
  "confidence": "high",
  "compatibility": {
    "observedReleases": [
      "8.62.09"
    ],
    "knownIncompatible": []
  },
